\f0\fs24 \cf2 The fireplace in the Green Room is one of the room\'92s most theatrical features and offers valuable insight into the work of the Bagatti Valsecchi brothers. To create this striking architectural element, they skillfully combined a 16th-century mantel with a decorative background bearing their own emblems. The result is a perfect fusion of Renaissance tradition and personal taste. The carved motifs they designed, preserved in the museum\'92s archive, include zoomorphic helmets and crossed shields, but not only those: the original drawing featured a screaming head, later replaced by entwined sea monsters surrounding a triton. Every element of the fireplace embodies power and mystery, a perfect expression of the brothers\'92 design spirit.}